+ *   g smmu gtest [valid]  G2b-1: which of the six stream groups take writes? A value that differs from the current one,
+ *                     then restored; with "valid" the SMR written has VALID = 1 (for the GMU stream, id 5 mask 0x400)
+ *   g smmu clk        G2b-2: turn on gcc_ddrss_gpu_axi_clk, the "mem" clock of the SMMU that Linux enables before any access
  *   g r ADDR [N]      read N 32-bit words (default 1, at most 16) at the physical address ADDR (hex)
  * Windows: GCC 0x100000..0x1fffff always; gpucc 0x2c90000..0x2c98fff only while gcc_gpu_cfg_ahb_clk is running (reading
  * it with that clock off would hang the bus); the GMU 0x2c6a000..0x2c8ffff only once G1 has left it readable. Offsets and bits come from the Linux
@@ -196,7 +198,7 @@ gpu_wr_cc(uint32_t off, uint32_t val)
